  "J₁ is the first-order Bessel function, and h(0) = 1 by its limit. Its first positive zero is v ≈ 3.831706. Dividing by 2π gives 0.609835. The two-point image is h(√((x − d/2)² + y²)) + h(√((x + d/2)² + y²)).": "J₁ 是一阶贝塞尔函数，根据极限有 h(0) = 1。其第一个正零点为 v ≈ 3.831706；除以 2π 得到 0.609835。两点图像为 h(√((x − d/2)² + y²)) + h(√((x + d/2)² + y²))。",
  "04 / LOOK IN FREQUENCY SPACE": "04 / 观察频率空间",
